{"title":"1984 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 1984 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/8/9284c6f851f10cea8a4841d87d17f472e23d8b22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le yz+zx+xy-2xyz\\le{7\\over27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"241\" height=\"37\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are non-negative real numbers satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fce09322356796e6adce205b1e7d6d0b7d7e5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find one pair of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/c/6bc42dc09a2c161aa30be74d70a220c6acf924c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab(a+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/4283272ce32f552d3d1df227fd4b0b808b33016f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)^7-a^7-b^7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"19\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a00241b495a94bfc00453fb6d99d4123ace04e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^7$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> in the plane. Every point in the plane is colored with one of a finite number of colors. Given a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in the plane, the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34d0a6db39eb915264c507de9f74470a3e7c0136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(X)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> has center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bcbf1dd71b52e57e9d58e39f82ed67afbea288e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX+{\\angle AOX\\over OX}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"112\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49caec5d05517e11f8b6b07c43f0a35efcb31a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOX$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is measured in radians in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa914ed4bd30af60a82d993a58fafc8144fdf3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,2\\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that we can find a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, not on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, such that its color appears on the circumference of the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34d0a6db39eb915264c507de9f74470a3e7c0136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(X)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a convex quadrilateral with the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> being tangent to the circle on diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to the circle on diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> are parallel.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of the lengths of all the diagonals of a plane convex polygon with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> vertices (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d8a348130d140aad5a9c23958578539f753241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be its perimeter. Prove that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/a/59a9cef9ad189f08f3a0fa70b1523eccef98ea1a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n-3&lt;{2d\\over p}&lt;\\Bigl[{n\\over2}\\Bigr]\\cdot\\Bigl[{n+1\\over 2}\\Bigr]-2,\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"41\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bceb7b14e55d33a8bca29b7863ad3cdae95afce4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the greatest integer not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb60e0857a2c0a2c47acfbe81781032feb1f7150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be odd integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3dde70dfa7032f8dc030bce939e7954365990643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;a&lt;b&lt;c&lt;d$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"141\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48f321bf029f7fb84615b987e2aaebb96e2c1537.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ad=bc$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />. Prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbe17a75e168e5f6de3be64a6d4fb7be6310d0ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+d=2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84c1aeb3917188cdb5959f689199a3cbb4b746a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c=2^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" /> for some integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO\" title=\"1984 IMO\">1984 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1984\">IMO 1984 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO\" title=\"1979 IMO\">1979 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO\" title=\"1983 IMO\">1983 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO\" title=\"1985 IMO\">1985 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018042829\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 245/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 837/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7297/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.347      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.347      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20537:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018042829 and revision id 144013. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}